# Line endings are stored as LF inside the repository and written out in whatever form the
# machine checking them out prefers. Without this, files carry whatever the editor that wrote
# them produced: this repo was first committed with CRLF, while the machine's own git default
# is to convert on checkout, so a clone made here produced different bytes than the working
# copy it was cloned from. Harmless for a page a browser renders either way, but it turns the
# next edit of any file into a diff against every line of it.
* text=auto

# The published builds must never be touched by that conversion. Git detects binary content on
# its own and would skip them anyway; saying it out loud means a careless pattern above can
# never corrupt an 11MB APK into one that will not install.
*.apk binary
*.exe binary
